# Stray temp artifacts
temp_page.png
temp_*.png

# SOURCES LIVE IN ../sanskrit-texts-sources/ (DECISIONS 2026-07-17, enforced 2026-08-18).
# This repo holds the translation layer only: one JSON per text, plus the docs/ wiki. Raw
# Devanagari transcriptions (.md), OCR dumps (.txt) and scans (.pdf) were moved out
# wholesale; these patterns stop them coming back by accident. Markdown is deliberately NOT
# ignored — docs/ is tracked. The corpus tree itself now holds JSON only: the per-text and
# per-category readme files were drained 2026-09-02 into docs/INVENTORY.md and
# docs/CANONICAL_COUNTS.md.
*.pdf
*.txt
**/raw/

# ONE-SHOT TRANSLATION DRIVERS (2026-09-15). This repo's convention is already stated in
# CLAUDE.md — "Do not commit processing scripts (batch*.py, inject*.py etc.) ... they were
# throwaway tools" — but nothing enforced it, so 16 of them sat untracked and turned
# `git status` into noise that hid real changes. Ignored rather than deleted: they are the
# user's translation work, and scripts/apply_translations.py in particular holds ~33 KB of
# hand-curated Hindi as DATA, so deleting it would lose the provenance of translations that
# are now in the corpus.
#
# Deliberately NARROW. `translate_*` does NOT match the tracked `translation_audit.py` /
# `translation_backlog.py`, and `apply_translations.py` is named exactly so it cannot shadow
# the tracked `apply_phala.py`. Check with `git ls-files '*.py'` before widening either.
/translate_*.py
/retranslate_*.py
/test_sdk.py
scripts/translate_*.py
scripts/retranslate_*.py
scripts/apply_translations.py
scripts/run_all_translations.py
scripts/build_hindi_translations.py

# Virtualenvs. `.venv` is the TRANSLATION scripts' environment (Python 3.14 + google-generativeai)
# and predates this package; it is deliberately left alone. The package's own env is
# `.venv-corpus`, because pyproject.toml pins >=3.12,<3.14 and `uv sync` would otherwise
# REPLACE .venv rather than coexist with it. Neither belongs in git.
.venv/
.venv-corpus/
